From 4c17b8cf3430e5d32a56048db5766d0d9b52a657 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:02:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Detect Cursor cloud hosts; host is an automatic pick only
 with the marker

A Cursor cloud agent shell (CURSOR_AGENT=1 plus CLOUD_AGENT_*) lets a
host that is named as the primary or a backup run without
ROBOREV_HOST_AGENT. It never makes host an automatic pick or lists it:
only ROBOREV_HOST_AGENT=1 does both, and with it host is the non-strict
last resort when no agent is available. Without any marker nothing
changes unless config names host.

A named host without a marker fails fast with no retry or failover, and
a stored host backup is skipped with a note naming the marker. Only host
synthesis errors take the typed retry path; other agents keep theirs.
Doctor asks the daemon about host by name, so detection alone raises no
false marker warning. Host cannot classify or be a budget substitute.
